# lionturtle is Rust built without ThreadSanitizer instrumentation. TSan
# sees its memory accesses through libc's interceptors but none of its
# atomics or fences, so every value it hands between threads looks like a
# race, including bytes the store then reads in C++. These patterns drop
# any report with a lionturtle or Rust frame in either stack. Built with
# -Zsanitizer=thread, lionturtle's own tests report only its memtable
# B-tree's (bbtree) deliberate optimistic reads, which validate a node's
# version after reading it unlatched; with an instrumented lionturtle,
# race:bbtree:: would be the only suppression needed.
race:lionturtle/src/
race:crossbeam
race:parking_lot
race:/rustc/
